{
  "id": "jigsaw-method",
  "term": "jigsaw method",
  "definition": "The jigsaw method is a structured cooperative learning approach in which lesson material is split into different parts, each student learns one part, works with peers studying the same part, and then teaches it back to their original small group. It is designed to create mutual dependence and individual responsibility so that students must combine their pieces to learn the full lesson.",
